WEBVTT

1
00:00:02,293 --> 00:00:04,713
[♪ slow instrumental music playing]

2
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:10,051
[♪ "Brand New Day" by Demi Lovato playing]

3
00:00:12,637 --> 00:00:14,389
<i>♪ I'm gonna run so fast
till I can't breathe ♪</i>

4
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:15,473
<i>♪ I can't breathe ♪</i>

5
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>- ♪ Come along and follow me ♪
- ♪ Follow me ♪</i>

6
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:22,313
<i>♪ Let's make some noise
Like we never did before ♪</i>

7
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:26,735
<i>♪ It's a brand new day ♪</i>

8
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:28,194
<i>♪ Don't you see me ♪</i>

9
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,738
- Hey, come on, man.
- Sorry, sorry.

10
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:31,948
<i>♪ On my way ♪</i>

11
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,199
<i>♪ So completely ♪</i>

12
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:35,785
<i>♪ This time I'm gonna sing
and you're gonna hear it ♪</i>

13
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,954
<i>♪ This time I'm gonna show you
that I got the spirit ♪</i>

14
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:41,541
[over speakers] <i>♪ It's a brand new day ♪</i>

15
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:44,419
<i>♪ And I'm feelin' good ♪</i>

16
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:48,214
Oh, my God! Look, look,
there's the cabins.

17
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:50,592
And there's a stage over there. [chuckles]

18
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,469
We're here!

19
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:53,636
Finally.

20
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:57,474
I'm exactly where I'm supposed to be.

21
00:00:57,557 --> 00:00:59,100
[chuckles] Mom, Dad.

22
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:01,519
Literally all of our favorite artists
spent their summers here.

23
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:03,980
I mean, Camp Rock is basically
a historical landmark.

24
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:06,024
Thank you so much.

25
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:09,569
Well, we're just glad you two
get to spend more time together.

26
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:15,784
Mmm.

27
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:16,910
Sage, stop.

28
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:17,994
[Sage] Desi, come on.

29
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:19,913
How are you not geeking out right now?

30
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:22,040
I mean, this has been
our dream for, like, ever.

31
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:26,044
Is this how it's gonna be all of summer?

32
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,130
I mean, you barely even talking to me?

33
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:33,009
Well, I figured that's how you'd want it,
since you broke up the band.

34
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,596
Look, I know you

35
00:01:36,679 --> 00:01:40,183
and you're just as excited as I am
whether you admit it or not.

36
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:42,602
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

37
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,905
Cliff, son. Remember what we worked on.

38
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:55,532
Self-control in group settings, okay?

39
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:57,826
[imitating Yoda] "Control myself, I must!

40
00:01:57,909 --> 00:02:01,496
For in restraint true strength lies."

41
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:03,665
- Is that Yoda?
- Yeah.

42
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:07,752
[♪ upbeat rock music continues]

43
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:14,092
Um, Rosie, darling,
are-are we absolutely sure about this?

44
00:02:14,175 --> 00:02:17,095
You said I could come to Camp Rock
if I brought my cello.

45
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:19,222
[sighs]

46
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:28,857
Hey, guys. I'm Desi.

47
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:29,983
[♪ playing rock music]

48
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:34,154
Sick.

49
00:02:40,243 --> 00:02:41,286
- Hey.
- Hey.

50
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:42,787
Looks like we're bunkmates.

51
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,414
- I'm Sage.
- I'm Rosie.

52
00:02:44,497 --> 00:02:48,376
I called bottom bunk,
but the top bunk is all yours.

53
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:51,671
Could we discuss that? Actually, I'd love
the bottom bunk if possible.

54
00:02:51,754 --> 00:02:53,506
Sometimes I wake up and check on my cello,

55
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:55,091
you know, like people do
with their babies.

56
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,467
Huh.

57
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:59,804
Uh, you know what?

58
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:02,724
On second look, I might actually be able
to fit it up there with me, so...

59
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:04,726
No, no, no, no, no. No, it's okay.

60
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:08,146
I would never separate a girl from
her emotional support cello.

61
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:11,232
Trust me, I get it.
Look who came to camp with me.

62
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:13,151
- [Sage laughs]
- Thanks.

63
00:03:13,234 --> 00:03:15,153
[♪ drums beating in distance]

64
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:17,614
- [crowd chanting] Camp Rock!
- It can't be.

65
00:03:19,282 --> 00:03:20,825
Camp Rock!

66
00:03:22,118 --> 00:03:23,119
[chuckles]

67
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:24,204
Camp Rock!

68
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,288
[Sage] I can't believe
they still do this here.

69
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:26,623
- I thought it was a myth.
- Oh, yeah.

70
00:03:26,706 --> 00:03:29,042
Every year. Oh, I'm Callie Banks. Bunk 9G.

71
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:31,377
- No way, me too. I'm Sage.
- [crowd] Camp Rock!

72
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:33,922
So we just got done watching
the Camp Rock stomp.

73
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:35,632
Oh, my God, Maddie! We love you!

74
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:36,883
Maddie!

75
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,259
[Maddie] Hey.

76
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:42,138
- Wait, is that...
- "thatBaddieMaddie'09!"?

77
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,724
She has, like, a cabillion followers.

78
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,351
She thinks she runs this place.

79
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:47,727
Okay, let's dance.

80
00:03:47,810 --> 00:03:49,729
Yeah. Can you take this?

81
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:50,855
This too.

82
00:03:50,939 --> 00:03:52,815
She brought her backup dancers?

83
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:54,025
Maddie's Baddies?

84
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:56,236
[♪ upbeat music playing]

85
00:03:58,071 --> 00:03:59,822
She must be the best dancer here.

86
00:03:59,906 --> 00:04:01,991
Girl, not if I have
anything to say about it.

87
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,534
Okay.

88
00:04:03,618 --> 00:04:04,994
[Sage chuckles]

89
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:06,788
[♪ music continues]

90
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:14,545
[crowd cheering]

91
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:22,345
<i>♪ It's been a long and crazy road
but it led us back to home ♪</i>

92
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:25,598
<i>♪ What didn't kill us
Only made us stronger ♪</i>

93
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,684
<i>♪ We've been around the world and back ♪</i>

94
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:29,686
<i>♪ Lots of stories to unpack ♪</i>

95
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:32,772
<i>♪ Wanna hear 'em
You can come on over ♪</i>

96
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:36,442
<i>♪ Come over, come over ♪</i>

97
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:40,196
<i>♪ If you can hear it
you can come on over ♪</i>

98
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:42,532
<i>♪ On a long and crazy road ♪</i>

99
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:43,950
<i>- ♪ But it led us back to home ♪</i>
- [grunts]

100
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,535
- Dude!
- What?

101
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:47,203
- You keep crossing me.
- [Lark] Cut!

102
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:48,288
[bell ringing]

103
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:49,998
So, so great, guys.

104
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:52,083
Yeah, loved when you all gave up at once.

105
00:04:52,166 --> 00:04:53,584
Let's take ten!

106
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:56,087
No, you've gotta be kidding me.

107
00:04:56,170 --> 00:04:57,839
[♪ upbeat music playing]

108
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:00,717
Hey, Lark.

109
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,844
[sighs] Hi, Shane. Hi.

110
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,806
You good? You seem, um,
more overly caffeinated than normal.

111
00:05:06,889 --> 00:05:09,100
I'm fine. The tour is fine,
everything's fine.

112
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:10,560
[inhales] Okay, fine.

113
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:12,687
Girl Vibe is no longer available.

114
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:14,731
- Our opening act quit?
- They didn't quit, they broke up.

115
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:17,400
- They said their vibe was off.
- The vibe was off?

116
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:19,861
Jason and Nate are barely speaking
and they're here.

117
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:21,779
- [both] Yeah.
- We need to figure this out

118
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:23,448
or we're in serious trouble.

119
00:05:23,531 --> 00:05:25,325
Okay, I'll just find us a new opening act.

120
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:28,411
No, you found Girl Vibe
and we saw how that turned out.

121
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:29,495
Yeah.

122
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:30,580
We'll handle the opening act
this time, okay?

123
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:32,790
Somebody had to do it.
You were out there being

124
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,626
Mr. Bigshot movie star
and Jason was in dad mode.

125
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:38,838
What? I am fully prepared
to rock all the time.

126
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:40,673
Hard to rock with a baby
strapped to your chest, okay?

127
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:41,758
- She knows how to rock.
- And you,

128
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:43,634
by the way, do you even know
the words to this song?

129
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:45,303
Why are you always wearing stripes
when I'm wearing stripes?

130
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:47,513
I'm not wearing stripes
all the time. This is a one time--

131
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:48,890
Enough!

132
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:53,436
We are about to begin a sold out
national tour called Reconnected.

133
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:55,855
It's gonna blow up in our faces when
you're this disconnected.

134
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:58,816
First things first,
you guys need to find a new opening act.

135
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,152
I think I know just the place.

136
00:06:01,235 --> 00:06:02,528
[♪ upbeat music playing]

137
00:06:02,612 --> 00:06:04,781
Welcome to Camp Rock!

138
00:06:04,864 --> 00:06:07,158
[all cheering]

139
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:11,245
Let me ask you something.
Who's ready for the best summer ever?

140
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,914
[all continue cheering]

141
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:15,708
I'm Connie Torres, camp director.

142
00:06:16,376 --> 00:06:19,170
And yes, Mitchie's Mom.

143
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:22,548
This camp changed Mitchie's life.

144
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:26,761
And now I run it, which means I get
a chance to watch it change yours.

145
00:06:26,844 --> 00:06:28,012
[crowd cheering]

146
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:31,474
Couple quick rules, most important...

147
00:06:32,975 --> 00:06:33,976
no phones.

148
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:36,270
- [all groan]
- I know, I know.

149
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:40,483
But Camp Rock is better face to face
than screen to screen.

150
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:42,110
Trust me.

151
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:44,654
- [scoffs]
- You know, when I look out at all of you,

152
00:06:44,737 --> 00:06:49,075
all I can think about is all the talent
that has come through Camp Rock.

153
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:51,577
Legends are made here.

154
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:55,331
And I know that this summer
will be no different!

155
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:57,250
[all cheering]

156
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:58,668
- [engine revving]
- [gasps]

157
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,503
[♪ upbeat music playing]

158
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:10,138
[chattering indistinctly]

159
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:18,813
And speaking of Camp Rock legends,
let's welcome back Connect 3!

160
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:20,148
[all cheering]

161
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:21,399
- Are you kidding?
- What?

162
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:23,609
It's Shane Gray, it's Shane Gray.

163
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:28,072
- [♪ upbeat music playing]
- What's up Camp rock?

164
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:29,782
[cheering continues]

165
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:32,118
- Hello, campers.
- How's it going, campers?

166
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:35,663
Hi!

167
00:07:36,247 --> 00:07:37,498
Good to see you.

168
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:39,375
[Connie] Here you go.

169
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:40,751
Camp Rock.

170
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:42,044
Man, I've missed this place.

171
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,796
Yeah, it is so good to be back.

172
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,381
[crowd cheering]

173
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,758
All right, let's get into
why we're here, shall we?

174
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:48,885
We have a big year ahead.

175
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:50,720
Thirty cities, sold out tour.

176
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:52,847
Crowd so loud,
you can't hear yourself think.

177
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:55,057
The only thing missing...

178
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,392
someone to open for us.

179
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,269
Ah, but not just any opener.

180
00:07:58,352 --> 00:07:59,604
Someone reliable,

181
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,565
who won't change the set list
five minutes before showtime.

182
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:04,984
[chuckles politely]
Somebody who shows up on time.

183
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:07,278
Who doesn't need three assistants
to tune one guitar.

184
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:09,780
Someone who won't fall asleep
at rehearsals

185
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:12,366
because bedtime at home is now 8:30.

186
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:13,951
Wow, you're really doing this?

187
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:17,038
Anyway, we figured, why not come here

188
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:20,041
and find our opening act
right here, right now.

189
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:21,375
[camper] Yeah!

190
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,794
[Shane] All right, here's the deal.
Over the next two weeks,

191
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:26,088
there's going to be three challenges.

192
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:28,883
You get through those,
you get a shot at the Final Jam.

193
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:32,303
You will be performing
an original song written by you.

194
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:35,473
It's your chance to show us
exactly who you are.

195
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:38,309
And we're gonna be in the crowd to choose
our next tour mate.

196
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:40,603
So, no pressure,
just the chance of a lifetime

197
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:43,940
and eternal bragging rights
that you opened for Connect 3.

198
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:45,066
[cheering]

199
00:08:45,149 --> 00:08:46,234
Oh, my Gosh.

200
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:49,111
[Jason] Until then, you'll be
in the very capable hands

201
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:50,947
of our tour manager, Lark.

202
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:54,700
I am so getting a raise for this.

203
00:08:55,409 --> 00:08:57,495
All right, Camp Rock.

204
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:59,455
Who's ready to open for Connect 3?

205
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:00,706
[all cheering]

206
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,416
[♪ upbeat music playing]

207
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,126
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

208
00:09:06,295 --> 00:09:08,714
<i>♪ I was born with fire in my veins ♪</i>

209
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,592
<i>♪ Adrenaline's been screaming my name ♪</i>

210
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:14,220
<i>♪ And it's my time to shine ♪</i>

211
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:17,265
<i>♪ I've got my moves down
head up, hitting my mark ♪</i>

212
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:20,101
<i>♪ Face front, straight back
know it by heart ♪</i>

213
00:09:20,184 --> 00:09:23,020
<i>♪ And my eye's on the prize ♪</i>

214
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:26,315
<i>♪ Tour bus, flashing lights
save me a spot ♪</i>

215
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:28,943
<i>♪ Billboards, center stage ready or not ♪</i>

216
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:33,447
<i>♪ 'Cause I know
I could be one in a million ♪</i>

217
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:37,451
<i>♪ One shot this is the moment ♪</i>

218
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:39,662
<i>♪ One chance
I'm gonna show them ♪</i>

219
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:43,583
<i>♪ Dream so close that I can touch it ♪</i>

220
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:46,002
<i>♪ One beat away
and I'm ready to crush it ♪</i>

221
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:48,754
<i>♪ One break not gonna slow down ♪</i>

222
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:52,008
<i>♪ Someday is happening right now ♪</i>

223
00:09:52,091 --> 00:09:55,094
<i>♪ Dream so close
I almost got it ♪</i>

224
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:58,097
<i>♪ One beat away and I'm ready to rock it ♪</i>

225
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:01,475
[siren chirps]

226
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:05,229
[♪ music continues]

227
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:19,827
[exhales]

228
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,914
<i>♪ Heartbeat racing loud in my chest ♪</i>

229
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:26,500
<i>♪ Whispers feed the fear in my head ♪</i>

230
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:29,128
<i>♪ But I'm not backing down ♪</i>

231
00:10:29,211 --> 00:10:31,005
<i>♪ Got my my game face</i>
<i>Deep breath</i> ♪

232
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:32,381
♪ <i>Keeping my cool ♪</i>

233
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:35,176
<i>♪ Straight lines, sharp turns
No other rules ♪</i>

234
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:37,762
<i>♪ I'm going to wear this crown ♪</i>

235
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:40,848
<i>♪ Sound check, limousine
Name on the door ♪</i>

236
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:43,517
<i>♪ Headline, VIPs
Screaming for more ♪</i>

237
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:48,939
<i>♪ 'Cause I know I can be
one in a million ♪</i>

238
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:51,901
<i>♪ One shot
This is the moment ♪</i>

239
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:55,071
<i>♪ One chance
I'm gonna show them ♪</i>

240
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:58,157
<i>♪ Dream so close that I can touch it ♪</i>

241
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,785
<i>♪ One beat away
and I'm ready to crush it ♪</i>

242
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:03,579
<i>♪ One break
Not gonna slow down ♪</i>

243
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,290
<i>♪ 'Cause someday is happening right now ♪</i>

244
00:11:06,957 --> 00:11:09,794
<i>♪ Dream so close
I almost got it ♪</i>

245
00:11:09,877 --> 00:11:12,838
<i>♪ One beat away and I'm ready to rock it ♪</i>

246
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:16,217
<i>♪ One shot ♪</i>

247
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:19,220
<i>♪ One chance ♪</i>

248
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:24,183
<i>♪ One beat away
One beat away ♪</i>

249
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:27,061
<i>♪ I want the spotlight
to shine in my eye ♪</i>

250
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:29,897
<i>♪ I wanna kick back and go with the vibe ♪</i>

251
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,941
<i>♪ One last dance and a stage ♪</i>

252
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:35,444
<i>♪ Making new beats
and new friends on the way ♪</i>

253
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:40,866
<i>♪ Right here is where I belong ♪</i>

254
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:43,703
<i>♪ One shot
This is the moment ♪</i>

255
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:46,580
<i>♪ One chance
I'm gonna show them ♪</i>

256
00:11:47,206 --> 00:11:50,042
<i>♪ Dream so close that I can touch it ♪</i>

257
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:52,795
<i>♪ One beat away
and I'm ready to crush it ♪</i>

258
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:55,464
<i>♪ One break
Not gonna slow down ♪</i>

259
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,341
[chorus] <i>♪ Someday is happening</i>
<i>Right now </i> ♪

260
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:58,426
<i>♪ No, no, no ♪</i>

261
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:01,512
<i>♪ Dream so close
I almost got it ♪</i>

262
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:04,598
<i>♪ One beat away and I'm ready to rock it ♪</i>

263
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:06,809
[both grunt]

264
00:12:07,643 --> 00:12:09,311
[♪ mellow guitar music playing]

265
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,692
[Connie] You must be Fletch Robinson?

266
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,486
Yeah. Yeah, I'm sorry I'm late.

267
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:18,988
Welcome to Camp Rock.

268
00:12:19,697 --> 00:12:21,782
You, sir, know how to make an entrance.

269
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,080
This way.

270
00:12:32,001 --> 00:12:33,627
[chattering indistinctly]

271
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:36,547
The older bunk was already full
when your cousin called.

272
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,633
- I'm fine wherever.
- Okay, good, good.

273
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:40,801
Because this bunk
is the one that's available.

274
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:41,969
[murmuring]

275
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:44,513
Boys, this is Fletch.

276
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:47,016
Fill him in on what he missed, okay?

277
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:49,351
All right.

278
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:55,858
Is it true you came
in a cop car from jail?

279
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,111
<i>♪ Fletch go fetch ♪</i>

280
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,571
<i>♪ Fletch I bet you wanna play catch ♪</i>

281
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:02,907
<i>♪ Fletcha, Fletch! Fletch, catch this! ♪</i>

282
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,911
I'm Cliff.

283
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:11,749
[sighs]

284
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:15,544
[gasping]

285
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:17,713
Relax.

286
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:20,174
If I wanted to hurt you...

287
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:23,010
I'd wait till lights out.

288
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:28,516
<i>♪ One shot
This is the moment ♪</i>

289
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:31,435
<i>♪ One chance
I'm gonna show them ♪</i>

290
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:34,939
<i>♪ Dreams so close
I almost got it ♪</i>

291
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:37,691
<i>♪ One beat away
And I'm ready to rock it ♪</i>

292
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:39,693
- Yes! Sing it, girl!
- [gasps] Oh.

293
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:44,156
No, that wasn't singing,
that was, um, vowel support.

294
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,451
A technical exercise
like scales or Pilates.

295
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,662
It sounded like singing to me.

296
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:53,207
Impossible. I come from a long line
of classical musicians.

297
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:56,210
My parents forbid me from indulging in
recreational melody.

298
00:13:56,293 --> 00:13:57,294
It leads to...

299
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:59,505
- [whispers] ...jazz.
- Call it what you want,

300
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:01,173
but it sounded good.

301
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:04,468
And I look forward to competing against
your vocal Pilates.

302
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:06,136
[chuckles] No, I am not competing.

303
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,596
Um, I'm a cello player.

304
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,432
I'm like the Wi-Fi,
essential but unnoticed.

305
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:11,976
Well, log in, girl.

306
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:14,186
I mean, I still plan on winning,

307
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:17,398
but it's not a real competition without
some real competition.

308
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:18,524
Me?

309
00:14:19,191 --> 00:14:20,234
Singing?

310
00:14:21,318 --> 00:14:24,238
I don't know. It just feels
so front and center.

311
00:14:24,321 --> 00:14:26,198
You know, with a cello,
you're the foundation,

312
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:28,117
the candlestick supporting the flame.

313
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:30,953
To actually be the flame?

314
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:35,207
- I could never.
- I mean, you do you.

315
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,418
But news flash, this is Camp Rock.

316
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:40,421
Around here, even the candlesticks sing.

317
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:46,093
<i>♪ We talk the talk
We're the kids of Camp Rock ♪</i>

318
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:49,346
<i>♪ We walk the walk</i>
<i>We talk the talk</i> ♪

319
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:51,974
♪ <i>We're the kids of Camp Rock ♪</i>

320
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:53,934
[all] Whoo!

321
00:14:59,398 --> 00:15:01,400
- You lose something?
- Yeah.

322
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:03,736
Yeah. Uh... Uh... Uh...

323
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:05,112
Drumsticks! The guys thought

324
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:06,697
it'd be hilarious
to chuck 'em on the roof.

325
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,366
[sighs] Message received.

326
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:19,084
- [thumps]
- [rattling]

327
00:15:22,671 --> 00:15:23,672
- Thanks.
- [drumsticks clatter]

328
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:24,840
[whispers] Yeah.

329
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:28,302
<i>♪ Bounce to the beat
Bounce, bounce to the beat ♪</i>

330
00:15:28,385 --> 00:15:29,845
<i>♪ Bounce to the beat
Bounce, bounce to the beat ♪</i>

331
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:30,930
<i>♪ Bounce to the beat... ♪</i>

332
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:33,849
Yo, that's been in my head
since breakfast. Do you ever get that?

333
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,225
Yeah, actually, I do.

334
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:38,062
Well, I'm gonna use it,
write the whole song,

335
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:40,230
perform it, win, tour.

336
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,315
Boom!

337
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:42,942
New life.

338
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,443
Good luck with that, buddy.

339
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:45,736
Buddy?

340
00:15:45,819 --> 00:15:48,155
Should we harmonize later,
or is it too soon?

341
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:49,323
[scoffs]

342
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:51,283
Okay, so, you know that girl Rosie?

343
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:53,243
The goddess with the cello?

344
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:56,121
She says that for safety issues,
she avoids all cliffs.

345
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,332
But that's just her way
of saying that she likes me.

346
00:15:58,415 --> 00:15:59,959
What's your take?

347
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,711
[♪ upbeat music playing]

348
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:10,469
[Connie] Come in.

349
00:16:10,552 --> 00:16:11,929
[♪ upbeat music stops]

350
00:16:15,182 --> 00:16:16,892
- Hi. Rosie, right?
- [Rosie] Hi.

351
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:20,396
Yes. I'd like to revise my workshop
registration, please.

352
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:24,274
Let's see. "Hard Rock Basics,

353
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:27,319
Songwriting, Center Stage 101."

354
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:28,404
Wow.

355
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:31,281
These are some adventurous choices.

356
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:33,993
You go, girl.

357
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:36,829
Consider your registration

358
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:38,330
- revised.
- [pen swishes]

359
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:41,041
Thank you very much.

360
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,126
[Connie chuckles lightly]

361
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:48,549
[Sage] Callie, I'm so excited
for this competition.

362
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:50,175
[chuckles] I have lots to do today.

363
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,386
But I still can't believe
you're not competing.

364
00:16:52,469 --> 00:16:54,388
Look, I know my strengths.

365
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:56,849
I could carry a tune but dance...

366
00:16:57,599 --> 00:16:59,268
[exhales] ...that's my real voice.

367
00:16:59,351 --> 00:17:01,103
But Lark asked me to be her assistant.

368
00:17:01,186 --> 00:17:02,938
I mean, what's the first challenge?

369
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:05,858
Sing Connect 3's biggest hit
and make it our own.

370
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:08,235
We get to show Lark who we are as artists.

371
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:09,862
[chuckles softly]

372
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:11,572
[♪ upbeat music playing]

373
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:14,033
Oh, practice rooms are open. Gotta go.

374
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,576
Okay, you got this.

375
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:20,122
[exhales]

376
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:22,082
Five, six, seven, eight.

377
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:25,586
One, two, three, four,
and five, six, seven, eight,

378
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:29,381
and one, two, three,
four, five, six, seven, eight, one...

379
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:30,507
Hey.

380
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:32,384
[scoffs]

381
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:35,846
Not to be the practice room police,
but there's a 30-minute limit.

382
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:37,473
Don't even worry about it, girl.

383
00:17:37,556 --> 00:17:38,682
[chuckles softly] Okay.

384
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:44,605
Thing is, she's next for the room
and then he's next after that.

385
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:48,734
So if I were you,
I'd try and find another room.

386
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:52,905
But I love your whole vibe,
it's giving... [inhales]

387
00:17:52,988 --> 00:17:54,073
...effort.

388
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:55,157
[snickering]

389
00:17:56,366 --> 00:17:59,620
Again. Five, six, seven, eight.

390
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,625
[♪ playing soulful chords]

391
00:18:09,296 --> 00:18:11,006
Hey, can I steal this room?

392
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,091
All the others are taken.

393
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,592
Hi, Sage. I'm doing good.

394
00:18:13,675 --> 00:18:14,760
How are you?

395
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:17,763
[exhales] Please, I really need it.

396
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:19,556
Let me think about it for a second.

397
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:22,142
- No.
- Desi.

398
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:24,269
Come on, you're just messing around.

399
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:25,604
I actually have to rehearse.

400
00:18:25,687 --> 00:18:26,897
The first challenge is tomorrow.

401
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:28,357
And how do you know I'm not competing?

402
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,067
Because every time I try
to get you to play

403
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,444
Battle of the Bands,
you call me a sellout with no soul.

404
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,279
Now, that does sound like me.

405
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:37,157
[♪ resumes playing piano]

406
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:38,242
[smacks] All right.

407
00:18:38,992 --> 00:18:41,286
I'm pulling the big sister card. Out, now.

408
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:44,540
Hey, if your fancy new music school
didn't prepare you for this competition,

409
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:46,917
I don't know what half an hour
in a practice room is gonna do.

410
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,002
You're still mad that I left the band
to go to Anthem.

411
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:50,337
I don't know what you're talking about.

412
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:52,548
I'm pretty sure
we sound better without you.

413
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:57,010
I'm gonna be Connect 3's opening act,
and nothing's gonna throw me off my game.

414
00:18:57,094 --> 00:18:58,095
Not even you.

415
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:00,639
Enjoy the room.

416
00:19:00,722 --> 00:19:03,142
[footsteps receding]

417
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:04,685
[door closes]

418
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:07,396
[PA chimes]

419
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:09,148
[Lark on PA] <i>All competing campers,</i>

420
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:11,733
<i>meet me in the dining hall
for the first challenge.</i>

421
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:13,318
<i>Let's see who you are as an artist.</i>

422
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,988
<i>I need vocals. I need star power.</i>

423
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,239
<i>I need coffee.</i>

424
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:21,410
[♪ upbeat instrumental rock music playing]

425
00:19:25,122 --> 00:19:26,123
Let's begin.

426
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,250
Who's first?

427
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:30,544
<i>♪ Turn on the radio ♪</i>

428
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:33,297
<i>♪ As loud as it can go ♪</i>

429
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:37,301
<i>♪ Wanna dance until
my feet can't feel the ground ♪</i>

430
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:41,388
<i>♪ Say goodbye to all my fears ♪</i>

431
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:44,266
<i>♪ One good song they disappear ♪</i>

432
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:48,687
<i>♪ And nothing in the world
can bring me down ♪</i>

433
00:19:50,105 --> 00:19:52,316
[awkwardly, out of tune]
<i>♪ Hand clapping earth-shaking ♪</i>

434
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:54,735
<i>♪ Heartbreaking there's no-- ♪</i>

435
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:59,281
[confidently] <i>♪ Faking what you feel</i>
<i>when you're right at home ♪</i>

436
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:00,532
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

437
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:04,077
<i>♪ Music's in my soul ♪</i>

438
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:08,999
<i>♪ I can hear it every day
and every night ♪</i>

439
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:11,877
<i>♪ It's the one thing on my mind ♪</i>

440
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:15,047
<i>♪ Music's got control ♪</i>

441
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:17,966
<i>♪ And I'm never letting go ♪</i>

442
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:19,509
[both] <i>♪ No, no ♪</i>

443
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:23,639
<i>♪ I just wanna play my music ♪</i>

444
00:20:24,806 --> 00:20:27,434
<i>♪ Got my six-string on my back ♪</i>

445
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:29,353
<i>♪ Don't need anything but that ♪</i>

446
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:30,812
<i>♪ Don't need anything but that ♪</i>

447
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:35,776
<i>♪ Everything I want is here with me ♪</i>

448
00:20:35,859 --> 00:20:38,237
[in operatic voice]
<i>♪ So forget that fancy car ♪</i>

449
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,031
[in techno voice]
<i>♪ I don't need to go that far ♪</i>

450
00:20:41,114 --> 00:20:44,910
[pop style singing] <i>♪ What's driving me</i>
<i>is following my dream ♪</i>

451
00:20:44,993 --> 00:20:46,954
[vocalizing] <i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

452
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:49,331
[awkwardly] <i>♪ Hand clapping earthshaking ♪</i>

453
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:50,791
[confidently] <i>♪ Heartbreaking ♪</i>

454
00:20:50,874 --> 00:20:53,335
<i>♪ There's no faking what you feel ♪</i>

455
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:55,754
[R&B style singing]
<i>♪ When you're on a roll ♪</i>

456
00:20:55,837 --> 00:20:57,464
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

457
00:20:57,547 --> 00:21:01,260
[pop style singing] <i>♪ Music's in my soul ♪</i>

458
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:02,844
[R&B style singing] <i>♪ I can hear it ♪</i>

459
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,639
[Latin American style singing]
<i>♪ Every day and every night ♪</i>

460
00:21:05,722 --> 00:21:08,350
<i>♪ It's the one thing on my mind ♪</i>

461
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:11,728
<i>- ♪ Music's got control ♪</i>
- [rapping] <i>♪ Music's got control y'all ♪</i>

462
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:14,064
<i>♪ Never let it go, no ♪</i>

463
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:19,111
[jazz style] <i>♪ Oh no, no I just wanna</i>
<i>play my music ♪</i>

464
00:21:19,194 --> 00:21:22,739
[rock style singing]
<i>♪ Music's got control ♪</i>

465
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:27,286
<i>♪ And I'm never letting go
No, no ♪</i>

466
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:29,913
<i>♪ I just wanna play my music ♪</i>

467
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:32,582
<i>♪ I just wanna play my music ♪</i>

468
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:35,502
<i>♪ All night long ♪</i>

469
00:21:35,585 --> 00:21:36,628
<i>♪ Yeah ♪</i>

470
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:42,968
Before I post the list
of campers moving on in the competition,

471
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:46,013
I would just like to say, you are seen.

472
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,347
You are enough.

473
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:49,433
Please don't freak out, 'kay?

474
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:54,438
[♪ upbeat instrumental rock music playing]

475
00:21:54,521 --> 00:21:56,398
Breathe, Luke, just think.

476
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:59,401
You'll have front row seats
to someone else's dreams coming true.

477
00:21:59,484 --> 00:22:01,278
[Luke sobbing]

478
00:22:01,361 --> 00:22:03,864
I mean, you'll get 'em next time.

479
00:22:03,947 --> 00:22:07,617
[Luke continues sobbing]

480
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:10,203
I'm so proud of you!

481
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:12,122
Wait one sec.

482
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:16,084
- Hi. [chuckles]
- Hey.

483
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:18,003
I'm just gonna steal him for a sec.

484
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:21,715
[sighs]

485
00:22:21,798 --> 00:22:23,550
Desi, what are you doing here?

486
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:25,844
What does it look like I'm doing?
I'm networking.

487
00:22:25,927 --> 00:22:27,387
You said you weren't even competing.

488
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:29,306
Uh, I performed, didn't I?

489
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:31,892
You crashed the auditions
in a hoodie with no plan.

490
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:34,269
Sage, you were born planning things.

491
00:22:34,353 --> 00:22:36,229
I was born playing things.

492
00:22:36,313 --> 00:22:37,314
It's not a competition.

493
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:39,066
This literally is a competition.

494
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:41,360
[scoffs] I'll see you
at the next challenge, sis.

495
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:43,195
Break a leg.

496
00:22:43,278 --> 00:22:44,696
Maybe even break two.

497
00:22:46,114 --> 00:22:47,199
For balance.

498
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:50,410
[scoffs] Ugh.

499
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:56,166
Hey, nice job back there.

500
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:58,877
- Thanks.
- But kind of stiff.

501
00:22:58,960 --> 00:22:59,961
[fan whirring]

502
00:23:00,045 --> 00:23:01,713
Loosen up and have fun with it.

503
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:02,881
'Kay?

504
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:04,758
'Kay.

505
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,350
Hello down there.

506
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:16,937
Any chance you guys could do me a solid
and go grab camp director, Connie?

507
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:18,313
Funny story,

508
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:20,190
I didn't think I was afraid of heights.

509
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:22,025
[yelling] Turns out I am.

510
00:23:25,153 --> 00:23:26,655
[in normal voice] Appreciate you guys.

511
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:29,825
[yelling] You're gonna get her, right?

512
00:23:30,867 --> 00:23:33,662
Welcome to Camp Rock's
songwriting workshop.

513
00:23:33,745 --> 00:23:36,832
This isn't a part of the competition,
but I think it could really help.

514
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:38,959
I have been wanting
to bring this next guy here

515
00:23:39,042 --> 00:23:40,544
for a while.

516
00:23:40,627 --> 00:23:42,963
He is an up-and-coming singer/songwriter

517
00:23:43,046 --> 00:23:46,466
and one of the most-streamed artists
of all last year.

518
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:49,594
He's also one of my favorite
Camp Rock alums.

519
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:50,804
Please welcome...

520
00:23:50,887 --> 00:23:52,973
Calvin Rhodes!

521
00:23:53,056 --> 00:23:54,683
[crowd applauding and cheering]

522
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:55,976
Hi, Connie.

523
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:57,477
- Amazing.
- [Connie chuckling]

524
00:23:57,561 --> 00:23:59,479
Welcome, future legends.

525
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:00,981
I can't believe this is happening.

526
00:24:01,064 --> 00:24:02,441
His last album changed my life.

527
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:04,818
Songwriting is all in the details, okay?

528
00:24:04,901 --> 00:24:06,945
It's about the feeling under the feeling.

529
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:08,405
Don't tell me that she smiled.

530
00:24:08,488 --> 00:24:12,576
Tell me that her smile
holds the promise of a thousand dreams.

531
00:24:15,829 --> 00:24:16,955
Let's start smaller. Okay.

532
00:24:17,038 --> 00:24:18,874
Let's pair up
and let's interview each other.

533
00:24:18,957 --> 00:24:21,710
No. No, no, no, no, no.
Don't think you're getting off that easy.

534
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:24,713
I want you to interview
a camper that you haven't met before.

535
00:24:24,796 --> 00:24:27,549
Now, really ask
the weird questions, dig deep,

536
00:24:27,632 --> 00:24:29,009
find out what makes them tick.

537
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:30,969
Turn to the camper behind you.

538
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:33,013
Back row. Turn to the camper
on your right.

539
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:39,186
[♪ romantic guitar music playing]

540
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:41,313
- Hey.
- Hey.

541
00:24:42,647 --> 00:24:45,442
Five, six, seven, turn.

542
00:24:47,068 --> 00:24:48,153
Eight.

543
00:24:48,653 --> 00:24:50,489
Hey, Desi, no songwriting for you?

544
00:24:51,072 --> 00:24:52,574
No. Workshops aren't for me.

545
00:24:53,783 --> 00:24:55,035
You want to be a stand-in?

546
00:24:55,118 --> 00:24:56,870
I need help figuring out this transition.

547
00:24:56,953 --> 00:24:59,039
Pass, I am not a dancer.

548
00:24:59,122 --> 00:25:01,750
Well, if you want to open for Connect 3,
you kinda have to dance.

549
00:25:01,833 --> 00:25:03,710
Nah, I'll stick with what I know.

550
00:25:03,793 --> 00:25:06,004
Wow. King of the comfort zone.

551
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:08,340
Well, if you change your mind,
you know where to find me.

552
00:25:10,008 --> 00:25:11,218
[exhales]

553
00:25:13,303 --> 00:25:15,096
All right, let's get started.

554
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:16,264
Um...

555
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:19,017
You, tell me what you learned
about your partner.

556
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:23,021
Okay, um, hi, so my partner was Rosie.

557
00:25:23,104 --> 00:25:25,815
Her favorite color
is off-white but not beige.

558
00:25:25,899 --> 00:25:29,778
Her superpower is memorizing
every wrong note she has ever played,

559
00:25:29,861 --> 00:25:32,113
and her favorite pet is her metronome.

560
00:25:33,615 --> 00:25:35,116
- Nailed it.
- Yes!

561
00:25:35,992 --> 00:25:37,953
- [Calvin] See, that's proof right there...
- Good job.

562
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:40,038
...that you don't need fireworks
to light someone up.

563
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:43,291
Simple words,
real details, that's the goal.

564
00:25:44,042 --> 00:25:45,168
All right. Next volunteer.

565
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:47,712
[smacks lips]

566
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:49,422
Hey, "Mr. Please-don't-look at me."

567
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:55,220
I'm looking at ya.

568
00:25:57,222 --> 00:25:58,974
Okay, um...

569
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:01,476
Well, this is Sage Scott.

570
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:04,020
Hi. [chuckles]

571
00:26:04,104 --> 00:26:05,689
[Fletch] And as she just demonstrated,

572
00:26:05,772 --> 00:26:09,150
her nose sort of crinkles when she laughs.

573
00:26:09,234 --> 00:26:11,736
She also kinda sings
a little when she talks.

574
00:26:13,154 --> 00:26:16,074
And she bites her cuticles,
or tries to make a joke

575
00:26:16,825 --> 00:26:18,493
anytime she doesn't wanna
talk about something.

576
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:26,293
Hey, I've been messing with this...

577
00:26:26,376 --> 00:26:28,628
this melody for a little while now.

578
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:30,964
I've never really had
any lyrics that felt right.

579
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:34,551
But I think I do now.

580
00:26:37,304 --> 00:26:39,723
- Could I?
- Please do.

581
00:26:39,806 --> 00:26:41,641
[indistinct chatter]

582
00:26:56,906 --> 00:26:58,992
One, two, three, four.

583
00:26:59,075 --> 00:27:03,663
<i>♪ Mmm ♪</i>

584
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:09,377
<i>♪ Mmm ♪</i>

585
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:13,715
<i>♪ Crooked smile in a campfire light ♪</i>

586
00:27:13,798 --> 00:27:18,970
<i>♪ Eyes like embers under moonlit skies ♪</i>

587
00:27:19,054 --> 00:27:23,516
<i>♪ She don't notice
but she shines so bright ♪</i>

588
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:28,229
<i>♪ She's confident
but part of her is terrified ♪</i>

589
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:31,316
<i>♪ She thinks no one gets it but I do ♪</i>

590
00:27:31,399 --> 00:27:33,735
<i>♪ The highs and lows
we've both been through ♪</i>

591
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:36,780
<i>♪ Waiting for someone to see it too ♪</i>

592
00:27:37,864 --> 00:27:42,577
<i>♪ Maybe tomorrow we'll wake up
on the bright side ♪</i>

593
00:27:42,661 --> 00:27:44,913
<i>♪ Chase away all the dark nights ♪</i>

594
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:46,748
<i>♪ And find a way to hope ♪</i>

595
00:27:47,874 --> 00:27:50,001
<i>♪ Maybe tomorrow ♪</i>

596
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,379
<i>♪ We'll feel something so brand new ♪</i>

597
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:55,006
<i>♪ Leave our past in the rear view ♪</i>

598
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:57,717
<i>♪ And say it's gonna get better ♪</i>

599
00:27:57,801 --> 00:28:01,513
<i>♪ Maybe tomorrow, tomorrow ♪</i>

600
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:06,768
<i>♪ Maybe tomorrow, tomorrow ♪</i>

601
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:09,020
[all cheering]

602
00:28:09,104 --> 00:28:10,772
[all clapping]

603
00:28:13,149 --> 00:28:15,735
That is how you write a song.

604
00:28:15,819 --> 00:28:17,987
[clapping continues]

605
00:28:19,989 --> 00:28:22,534
Okay, so maybe I am
mildly in love with him

606
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:25,662
but like in a stupid way
that'll make a great song later.

607
00:28:25,745 --> 00:28:27,789
Not like a real way
where I'd ever focus on a guy

608
00:28:27,872 --> 00:28:30,333
I'm only gonna know for a couple of weeks
and divert all my attention

609
00:28:30,417 --> 00:28:32,168
from a competition that
could change my whole life.

610
00:28:32,252 --> 00:28:34,003
[chuckles softly]

611
00:28:34,087 --> 00:28:37,090
I just asked how
the workshop went, but okay.

612
00:28:37,173 --> 00:28:39,884
Also, I know he liked you I mean, hello.

613
00:28:39,968 --> 00:28:42,846
You said he told all of camp
that your nose crinkles! [squealing]

614
00:28:42,929 --> 00:28:43,930
[both laughing]

615
00:28:44,013 --> 00:28:46,474
[whispering] Also I heard
he's banned from most of Canada

616
00:28:46,558 --> 00:28:48,184
and the entire state of New Jersey.

617
00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:49,519
What?

618
00:28:50,687 --> 00:28:52,188
It doesn't matter anyway.

619
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:53,314
He's my competition.

620
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:55,650
I... I would never...

621
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:57,110
And there's the crinkles.

622
00:28:57,193 --> 00:28:58,194
[both laughing]

623
00:28:58,278 --> 00:29:00,655
It's involuntary, like, hiccups.

624
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:03,533
All right, we're going
to the bonfire. Let's go.

625
00:29:03,616 --> 00:29:04,659
You go.

626
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:06,703
I need to, like, get in the zone
for the second challenge.

627
00:29:06,786 --> 00:29:08,538
Come on!

628
00:29:08,621 --> 00:29:11,082
I just wish I knew what more I could do.

629
00:29:11,166 --> 00:29:15,754
I mean, I rehearse constantly
and then Lark says I'm too polished,

630
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:17,297
that I need to have more fun.

631
00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:22,010
So now I'm thinking I set aside 20 minutes
every day to just be carefree.

632
00:29:22,093 --> 00:29:23,720
You want to know what I love about dance?

633
00:29:23,803 --> 00:29:24,804
Hmm.

634
00:29:24,888 --> 00:29:27,766
That moment, I just stop thinking
and the beat takes over.

635
00:29:28,641 --> 00:29:31,102
When it's not about
nailing every move anymore.

636
00:29:31,686 --> 00:29:33,813
It's about being real enough
to make people feel it with me.

637
00:29:35,190 --> 00:29:37,150
And maybe that's what your music needs.

638
00:29:37,233 --> 00:29:38,902
It doesn't need more practice.

639
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:40,695
It needs more you.

640
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:41,946
[sighs]

641
00:29:42,530 --> 00:29:43,531
Okay, fine. I'll go.

642
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:45,784
[smacks lips] Okay,
I'll meet you out there.

643
00:29:45,867 --> 00:29:48,953
Oh, save me a seat with a backrest
before all the percussion kids snag them.

644
00:29:49,037 --> 00:29:50,538
- I got you.
- Thanks.

645
00:29:53,792 --> 00:29:55,126
[door creaks]

646
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:57,921
[door closes]

647
00:30:03,009 --> 00:30:04,010
[floorboard creaking]

648
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:07,096
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

649
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:08,556
[creaks again]

650
00:30:23,988 --> 00:30:24,989
[blows]

651
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:28,618
[sighs softly]

652
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:29,869
[laughing]

653
00:30:29,953 --> 00:30:31,371
Oh my gosh.

654
00:30:31,913 --> 00:30:34,165
[fire crackling]

655
00:30:38,378 --> 00:30:39,629
Hey.

656
00:30:39,712 --> 00:30:40,797
Hey.

657
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:43,800
[Rosie sighs]

658
00:30:43,883 --> 00:30:47,136
I've been thinking about doing something.

659
00:30:48,638 --> 00:30:50,431
It's not what people expect from me.

660
00:30:51,474 --> 00:30:53,393
It's not even what I expected from me.

661
00:30:55,311 --> 00:30:58,106
And, uh, it scares me.

662
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:02,026
In a good way.

663
00:31:03,778 --> 00:31:05,780
Is it... [whispers] ...murder?

664
00:31:08,366 --> 00:31:10,577
No, Cliff, it's not murder.

665
00:31:10,660 --> 00:31:12,078
Then you're good!

666
00:31:12,161 --> 00:31:13,162
Seriously.

667
00:31:13,246 --> 00:31:16,040
If it comes from the real you,
it's gonna be amazing.

668
00:31:20,086 --> 00:31:21,087
[exhales]

669
00:31:21,170 --> 00:31:23,131
Have you ever heard of the bagworm moth?

670
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:27,218
No? Okay, so the female
builds this little house

671
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:30,680
out of silk and twigs,
carries it everywhere.

672
00:31:30,763 --> 00:31:32,849
She hides in it her whole life.

673
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:34,309
But when she's ready...

674
00:31:35,768 --> 00:31:37,103
she just burns it down and flies.

675
00:31:39,272 --> 00:31:42,025
So, your pep talk is...

676
00:31:42,108 --> 00:31:43,526
"Don't be a worm?"

677
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:47,030
My pep talk is "Don't hide.

678
00:31:48,156 --> 00:31:49,574
Not when you've got wings."

679
00:31:53,328 --> 00:31:54,412
Thanks, Cliff.

680
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:55,580
Anytime.

681
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:58,917
Oh, uh, just checking.

682
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:01,377
Still not in love with me though, right?

683
00:32:01,461 --> 00:32:02,879
[laughs]

684
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:04,714
Give it time.

685
00:32:05,340 --> 00:32:06,549
Girls love a project.

686
00:32:07,050 --> 00:32:08,301
[laughs]

687
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:10,887
[phone ringing]

688
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:13,765
[sighs] Come on.

689
00:32:15,141 --> 00:32:17,101
Oh, the rocks. So cliche.

690
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:18,186
[Shane over phone] <i>Hey, Lark.</i>
<i>What's going on?</i>

691
00:32:18,269 --> 00:32:19,270
Shane, hi.

692
00:32:19,354 --> 00:32:21,814
Oh... Yes! Finally.

693
00:32:22,482 --> 00:32:23,858
How is the reconnecting going?

694
00:32:23,942 --> 00:32:26,319
Please tell me you guys are bursting
with brotherly love.

695
00:32:26,402 --> 00:32:27,737
[Shane] <i>Well, we're at least talking</i>
<i>to each other.</i>

696
00:32:27,820 --> 00:32:28,821
[Nate] <i>On a trial basis.</i>

697
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:30,531
- I'll take it.
<i>- How's the competition going?</i>

698
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:31,616
[signal breaking up]

699
00:32:31,699 --> 00:32:34,953
No, no, no, no, no, no, no. Hello? What?

700
00:32:35,036 --> 00:32:36,537
[Nate] <i>I said,</i>
<i>how's the competition going?</i>

701
00:32:36,621 --> 00:32:38,122
Really good, actually.

702
00:32:38,206 --> 00:32:41,793
Yeah. Tomorrow is the second challenge,
it's gonna be all about performance.

703
00:32:41,876 --> 00:32:45,171
I'm trying to find you guys
a triple threat opening act,

704
00:32:45,254 --> 00:32:48,049
singing, dancing, star power.

705
00:32:48,132 --> 00:32:50,259
[Nate] <i>Love it. By the end</i>
<i>of this challenge, let's get down</i>

706
00:32:50,343 --> 00:32:51,344
<i>to our final five competitors.</i>
[breaking up]

707
00:32:51,427 --> 00:32:52,428
What?

708
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:54,263
<i>And make sure they have
the right attitude while performing.</i>

709
00:32:54,347 --> 00:32:56,975
- [bees buzzing]
<i>- No matter what happens on stage,</i>

710
00:32:57,058 --> 00:32:58,101
<i>the show must go on.</i>

711
00:32:58,184 --> 00:32:59,477
[Jason] <i>What are you trying to say, Nate?</i>

712
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:01,396
[Nate] <i>What do you think</i>
<i>I'm trying to say, Jason?</i>

713
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:03,564
Yeah, right attitude, final five.

714
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:05,483
Copy that. I gotta go, guys.

715
00:33:05,566 --> 00:33:08,987
[♪ playing rock guitar chords]

716
00:33:14,534 --> 00:33:15,702
Sounds good.

717
00:33:15,785 --> 00:33:16,786
Thanks, man.

718
00:33:16,869 --> 00:33:18,997
- You mind if I jump in?
- Let's do it.

719
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,957
'Kay. Where does it start?

720
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:22,125
- Right there.
- [♪ plays riff]

721
00:33:23,042 --> 00:33:24,210
[♪ both jamming]

722
00:33:50,069 --> 00:33:52,447
That right there
is why I love music. [laughs]

723
00:33:52,530 --> 00:33:54,949
Same. That... That was awesome.

724
00:33:55,658 --> 00:33:58,036
A true jam sesh, just messing around.

725
00:33:58,119 --> 00:34:00,997
Jamming is great.
But I'm not here to mess around.

726
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:02,707
Ugh, you sound like Sage.

727
00:34:03,374 --> 00:34:04,625
Knew I liked her.

728
00:34:04,709 --> 00:34:06,794
Dude, don't talk about
my sister like that.

729
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:08,337
You telling me what to do?

730
00:34:08,421 --> 00:34:09,964
No, sir.

731
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:11,049
[chuckles softly]

732
00:34:13,718 --> 00:34:15,803
[PA chimes]

733
00:34:15,887 --> 00:34:17,722
[Connie over PA] <i>Time to rock and roll!</i>

734
00:34:17,805 --> 00:34:20,099
<i>All those who've made it through
to the dance challenge,</i>

735
00:34:20,183 --> 00:34:21,726
<i>please report to the flagpole.</i>

736
00:34:23,770 --> 00:34:24,979
Is Lark here?

737
00:34:25,063 --> 00:34:26,147
[both] No.

738
00:34:28,691 --> 00:34:31,069
[male camper] At least three
of these people have lice.

739
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:32,320
You're doing that wrong.

740
00:34:35,281 --> 00:34:37,200
Good morning,

741
00:34:37,283 --> 00:34:40,953
is what I would say
if I was a morning person.

742
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:42,371
[campers laughing]

743
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:43,790
[male camper] She's not a morning person.

744
00:34:43,873 --> 00:34:48,377
So, last night,
we lost a couple of campers,

745
00:34:48,461 --> 00:34:50,254
thanks to a smuggled phone.

746
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:51,506
- [crowd gasps]
- No way.

747
00:34:51,589 --> 00:34:52,715
[Lark] Reminder.

748
00:34:52,799 --> 00:34:56,010
No phones, no posts, no leaks.

749
00:34:56,094 --> 00:34:59,222
This tour stays under wraps. You got it?

750
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:00,348
- Yes.
- Yeah.

751
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:02,266
My assistant Callie...

752
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:04,393
Technically I'm not
supposed to call her that.

753
00:35:04,477 --> 00:35:07,688
Camper Callie is gonna lead us
in this dance challenge.

754
00:35:07,772 --> 00:35:08,815
Grab a mic and a hat.

755
00:35:08,898 --> 00:35:10,024
Follow me if you can.

756
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:14,153
No hats. If I see a fedora, you're donezo.

757
00:35:14,237 --> 00:35:15,238
That's a threat!

758
00:35:15,321 --> 00:35:17,907
I'm judging for overall star power.

759
00:35:17,990 --> 00:35:19,700
You either got it or you don't.

760
00:35:19,784 --> 00:35:23,204
Dance like no one is watching
except I'll be watching,

761
00:35:23,287 --> 00:35:24,789
very closely.

762
00:35:24,872 --> 00:35:27,583
Finally, my expertise.

763
00:35:27,667 --> 00:35:31,796
If I tap you on the shoulder,
you are eliminated.

764
00:35:31,879 --> 00:35:33,798
After this, we'll be down
to our final five.

765
00:35:33,881 --> 00:35:35,174
Have fun.

766
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:38,094
- [♪ hip hop music playing]
- Ready?

767
00:35:39,595 --> 00:35:40,638
<i>♪ Come on! ♪</i>

768
00:35:41,597 --> 00:35:42,723
Let's go.

769
00:35:45,351 --> 00:35:47,145
<i>♪ First stop, hit the groove ♪</i>

770
00:35:47,228 --> 00:35:49,397
<i>♪ Let the music play ♪</i>

771
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:51,482
<i>♪ Next stop, everybody ♪</i>

772
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,359
<i>♪ It's time to celebrate ♪</i>

773
00:35:53,442 --> 00:35:55,111
<i>♪ Here we go so let your flow show ♪</i>

774
00:35:55,194 --> 00:35:57,446
<i>♪ Make the dreams you got become real ♪</i>

775
00:35:57,530 --> 00:35:59,198
<i>♪ Let's do this, let me hear you, now ♪</i>

776
00:35:59,282 --> 00:36:01,367
<i>♪ Show me how you feel ♪</i>

777
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:03,786
[chorus] <i>♪ Let's start, start</i>
<i>start the party ♪</i>

778
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:05,413
<i>♪ Come on, come on everyone ♪</i>

779
00:36:05,496 --> 00:36:07,707
<i>♪ Let's start, start start the party ♪</i>

780
00:36:07,790 --> 00:36:08,791
<i>♪ What you waiting for now? ♪</i>

781
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:10,459
- I'm sorry.
- I just--

782
00:36:10,543 --> 00:36:11,836
My condolences.

783
00:36:11,919 --> 00:36:13,838
<i>♪ Come on, come on live it up ♪</i>

784
00:36:13,921 --> 00:36:16,007
<i>♪ Let's start, start start the party ♪</i>

785
00:36:16,090 --> 00:36:18,176
<i>♪ I know you never gonna wanna stop ♪</i>

786
00:36:18,259 --> 00:36:23,764
<i>♪ Let the music take us to paradise ♪</i>

787
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:25,600
<i>♪ Just close our eyes ♪</i>

788
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:30,479
<i>♪ Feel the groove wanna shake us ♪</i>

789
00:36:30,563 --> 00:36:32,231
<i>♪ Everywhere and everybody ♪</i>

790
00:36:32,315 --> 00:36:34,734
<i>♪ Turn it up
Let's start the party ♪</i>

791
00:36:34,817 --> 00:36:36,569
<i>♪ Ooh ♪</i>

792
00:36:37,945 --> 00:36:41,282
<i>♪ Pump, pump, pump, pump, pump ♪</i>

793
00:36:41,365 --> 00:36:43,159
<i>♪ The party ♪</i>

794
00:36:43,242 --> 00:36:47,496
<i>♪ We got it rolling
Never slowing down ♪</i>

795
00:36:47,580 --> 00:36:51,167
<i>♪ Lights, camera, action
Start the party now ♪</i>

796
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:55,755
<i>♪ I know you're ready
There's no need to wait ♪</i>

797
00:36:55,838 --> 00:36:59,717
<i>♪ Now's the time for us to celebrate ♪</i>

798
00:37:01,928 --> 00:37:04,555
<i>♪ Start, start the party ♪</i>

799
00:37:04,639 --> 00:37:05,806
<i>♪ Let's do it ♪</i>

800
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:08,267
<i>♪ Start, start the party ♪</i>

801
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:11,437
<i>♪ Everybody now
Start, start the party ♪</i>

802
00:37:11,520 --> 00:37:14,690
- [Maddie gasps] Sage!
- [Sage] Desi, keep dancing.

803
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:16,484
You can't just stop dancing.

804
00:37:16,567 --> 00:37:17,777
What?

805
00:37:17,860 --> 00:37:19,487
- That's not fair.
- What? [groans]

806
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:22,114
<i>♪ What you waiting for now? ♪</i>

807
00:37:22,198 --> 00:37:23,199
Wait!

808
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:26,077
No matter what, the show must go on.

809
00:37:26,160 --> 00:37:27,787
No!

810
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:29,872
<i>♪ Let's start, start start the party ♪</i>

811
00:37:30,539 --> 00:37:32,083
<i>♪ Come on, come on everyone ♪</i>

812
00:37:32,166 --> 00:37:33,334
That's not fair! Maddie, Maddie, Maddie!

813
00:37:33,417 --> 00:37:34,460
<i>♪ Let's start, start start the party ♪</i>

814
00:37:34,543 --> 00:37:35,878
Get off of me!

815
00:37:35,962 --> 00:37:38,464
What'd you do? Maddie, come back.

816
00:37:38,547 --> 00:37:40,091
<i>♪ Come on, come on
Live it up ♪</i>

817
00:37:40,174 --> 00:37:42,176
<i>♪ Let's start, start start the party ♪</i>

818
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:43,594
<i>♪ I know you never gonna wanna ♪</i>

819
00:37:43,678 --> 00:37:44,762
<i>♪ Come on let me hear you holler ♪</i>

820
00:37:44,845 --> 00:37:46,430
<i>♪ Party's never ever gonna stop ♪</i>

821
00:37:46,514 --> 00:37:47,515
[all cheering]

822
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:50,017
And then there were five.

823
00:37:50,601 --> 00:37:51,686
[cheering continues]

824
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:55,231
I know.

825
00:37:55,314 --> 00:37:57,358
Desi, consider yourself lucky.

826
00:37:57,984 --> 00:38:00,111
I'd work on your dance moves
if I were you.

827
00:38:03,656 --> 00:38:05,408
- No, you did.
- No, you did.

828
00:38:05,491 --> 00:38:06,742
- [both laughing]
- I can't.

829
00:38:08,452 --> 00:38:09,453
[scoffing]

830
00:38:13,499 --> 00:38:16,168
I never thought Maddie the Baddie
would go down in a dance challenge.

831
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:18,587
And yet, balance is restored!

832
00:38:18,671 --> 00:38:19,714
[laughs]

833
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:21,632
Speaking of baddies...

834
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:23,718
Callie, don't even...

835
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:25,344
Okay, look, I'm not saying
your brother is cute.

836
00:38:25,428 --> 00:38:28,264
I'm just saying he's not, not cute.

837
00:38:28,347 --> 00:38:30,057
[gags] Absolutely not.

838
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:31,225
Stop.

839
00:38:32,101 --> 00:38:33,394
Sorry, we're closed.

840
00:38:33,477 --> 00:38:34,770
I actually came to talk to Callie.

841
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:37,523
Go ahead.

842
00:38:37,606 --> 00:38:38,733
Alone.

843
00:38:38,816 --> 00:38:39,900
Okay.

844
00:38:45,573 --> 00:38:46,741
[scoffs]

845
00:38:46,824 --> 00:38:48,951
You're a really good dancer.

846
00:38:49,035 --> 00:38:50,786
Agreed. Thank you.

847
00:38:51,537 --> 00:38:53,122
Me not so much.

848
00:38:53,205 --> 00:38:55,499
I was thinking
maybe you could help me out.

849
00:38:55,583 --> 00:38:58,878
Give me a few... [whispers] ...lessons.

850
00:38:58,961 --> 00:39:01,297
Wait, you want me to do what?

851
00:39:01,380 --> 00:39:02,840
Please don't make me say it again.

852
00:39:02,923 --> 00:39:04,050
So you're actually gonna compete?

853
00:39:04,133 --> 00:39:05,301
Baby steps, Callie.

854
00:39:05,384 --> 00:39:07,720
First, you gotta teach me how to dance.

855
00:39:07,803 --> 00:39:10,139
Okay. But I'm not gonna go easy on you.

856
00:39:10,931 --> 00:39:11,932
So get ready.

857
00:39:12,641 --> 00:39:13,726
Cooler by the fire pit.

858
00:39:15,811 --> 00:39:18,522
Come on! Don't eat all
the marshmallows, people.

859
00:39:18,606 --> 00:39:20,191
Save it for tonight.

860
00:39:20,274 --> 00:39:22,318
- [phone ringing]
- Why is it so hard?

861
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:23,903
[sighs]

862
00:39:24,403 --> 00:39:25,988
Hey, Nate. What's going on?

863
00:39:26,072 --> 00:39:28,074
Hey, Lark. Can you tell Shane
that the suits are happening.

864
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:29,158
<i>He listens to you.</i>

865
00:39:29,241 --> 00:39:30,284
- [phone ringing]
- Hang on.

866
00:39:30,368 --> 00:39:31,369
Hey, Shane.

867
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:33,204
Can you tell Nate
we're not dressing up as groomsmen.

868
00:39:33,287 --> 00:39:35,164
You guys know you can say this
to each other directly.

869
00:39:35,247 --> 00:39:37,041
<i>We tried. It got loud.</i>

870
00:39:37,124 --> 00:39:38,918
- [cell phone vibrates]
- Hang on!

871
00:39:39,001 --> 00:39:41,045
Jason, please tell me
this is not about wardrobe.

872
00:39:41,128 --> 00:39:42,296
- No.
- Fantastic.

873
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:44,131
- Have you seen my child?
- Jason!

874
00:39:44,673 --> 00:39:47,176
You know what?
I have had enough of you three.

875
00:39:47,259 --> 00:39:49,804
Gentlemen, this is not
a conference call I asked for.

876
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:51,806
<i>You are grown men. Use your words</i>

877
00:39:51,889 --> 00:39:52,890
with each other.

878
00:39:52,973 --> 00:39:54,725
I just want us to look like
we belong up there.

879
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:56,143
And I just want us to feel like us,

880
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:58,521
- not the version everyone expects.
- [Lark] <i>Figure it out, guys!</i>

881
00:39:58,604 --> 00:40:00,773
I'm about to produce
a bonfire for the first time.

882
00:40:00,856 --> 00:40:02,650
And yes, there is a learning curve.

883
00:40:02,733 --> 00:40:03,859
[sighs] I'm hanging up.

884
00:40:03,943 --> 00:40:04,944
Wait, wait, wait.
How's the competition going?

885
00:40:05,027 --> 00:40:06,028
<i>Great.</i>

886
00:40:06,112 --> 00:40:07,321
<i>We're down to our final five.</i>

887
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:09,532
We just need to make sure they can really
handle being on tour.

888
00:40:09,615 --> 00:40:13,244
Exactly. A successful tour is about
more than just talent.

889
00:40:13,327 --> 00:40:14,578
[Jason] <i>Yeah. Long nights,</i>

890
00:40:14,662 --> 00:40:17,915
tight spaces, terrible food.
They gotta be able to survive the grind.

891
00:40:17,998 --> 00:40:19,125
And if they can handle that,

892
00:40:19,208 --> 00:40:20,709
they can pretty much handle
being on the road.

893
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:23,087
Hmm. No, not again.

894
00:40:23,170 --> 00:40:24,213
Oh, uh, update,

895
00:40:24,296 --> 00:40:26,257
- I found the baby.
- Great.

896
00:40:26,340 --> 00:40:27,716
You know what? I gotta go.

897
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:31,011
Canela. No, Emmy, drop the marshmallows!

898
00:40:31,804 --> 00:40:34,515
[Sage singing] <i>♪ Most days I am inspired ♪</i>

899
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:38,144
<i>♪ Some days I am awake ♪</i>

900
00:40:38,227 --> 00:40:39,395
[♪ guitar strums]

901
00:40:39,478 --> 00:40:44,900
<i>♪ I'm confident and insecure
even at my best ♪</i>

902
00:40:44,984 --> 00:40:46,152
Not bad.

903
00:40:46,235 --> 00:40:47,987
I'm still struggling with the lyrics.

904
00:40:49,321 --> 00:40:50,865
You just gotta have fun with it.

905
00:40:51,907 --> 00:40:53,742
[chuckles] You make it sound so easy.

906
00:40:59,039 --> 00:41:03,794
All right, just so you know,
all of this isn't gonna distract me.

907
00:41:03,878 --> 00:41:06,046
- All right? I'm in it to win it.
- So am I.

908
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:07,923
[chuckles softly]

909
00:41:09,717 --> 00:41:11,469
Can I ask you something?

910
00:41:11,552 --> 00:41:13,137
What's with you and your brother?

911
00:41:13,220 --> 00:41:14,472
[sighs]

912
00:41:15,264 --> 00:41:16,348
You picked up on that?

913
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:18,184
Yeah, it's kinda hard not to.

914
00:41:18,976 --> 00:41:20,603
We used to be in a band together,

915
00:41:21,687 --> 00:41:23,063
and then I left for Anthem.

916
00:41:24,356 --> 00:41:26,233
I wanted to take my music seriously.

917
00:41:27,067 --> 00:41:29,945
When the band broke up,
it kind of felt like we did, too.

918
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:33,491
[sighs]

919
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:36,243
Can I ask you something?

920
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:37,703
If you must.

921
00:41:37,786 --> 00:41:39,705
Are you really the bad boy
everyone says you are?

922
00:41:39,788 --> 00:41:40,956
Define bad.

923
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:43,042
You showed up to camp in a cop car.

924
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:44,585
[laughs]

925
00:41:46,086 --> 00:41:47,087
[clicks tongue]

926
00:41:50,132 --> 00:41:54,970
Um, truth is, I came straight from court.

927
00:41:56,931 --> 00:42:01,727
My mom passed away in March,
and it was always just me and her,

928
00:42:01,810 --> 00:42:03,604
and now it's just me.

929
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:05,356
[clicks tongue]

930
00:42:05,439 --> 00:42:07,024
A judge is figuring out where I go next.

931
00:42:08,692 --> 00:42:10,110
Fletch, I'm so sorry.

932
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:13,531
But I'm really glad you're here.

933
00:42:17,660 --> 00:42:20,120
[Cliff singing] <i>♪ Sage and Fletch</i>
<i>sitting in a-- ♪</i>

934
00:42:20,204 --> 00:42:21,580
Shoot!

935
00:42:21,664 --> 00:42:23,207
Guys, a little help?

936
00:42:24,583 --> 00:42:26,168
- You hungry?
- Starving.

937
00:42:26,794 --> 00:42:28,587
Come on. How am I supposed
to get back to shore?

938
00:42:28,671 --> 00:42:29,922
I can't swim.

939
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:31,257
[Fletch] Yeah, you can, Cliff.

940
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:33,217
[Cliff] I know I can. But I don't want to.

941
00:42:37,096 --> 00:42:38,430
- Stay vigilant.
- Mmm.

942
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:39,932
Revenge is near.

943
00:42:40,015 --> 00:42:41,058
[chuckles]

944
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:44,687
- Oh.
- It's a zombie. I still need to glaze it.

945
00:42:44,770 --> 00:42:45,938
Impressive.

946
00:42:46,021 --> 00:42:47,022
[clears throat]

947
00:42:47,731 --> 00:42:49,858
Maddie, can we go over the plan again?

948
00:42:50,442 --> 00:42:53,904
They each got the message
that Lark wanted a style consult.

949
00:42:54,863 --> 00:42:56,115
They'll be here any minute.

950
00:42:56,198 --> 00:42:58,784
- Wait, are you sure we shou--
- Don't gaslight me, Daniel.

951
00:42:58,867 --> 00:43:00,327
Mmm.

952
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:03,289
They sabotaged us in the dance challenge.

953
00:43:04,039 --> 00:43:05,207
We are not the problem here.

954
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:06,500
- Mmm-mmm.
- They are.

955
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:10,629
We bring joy to millions
with our joyful content that promotes joy.

956
00:43:11,255 --> 00:43:13,591
But somehow those five
are the chosen ones?

957
00:43:13,674 --> 00:43:14,842
I don't think so.

958
00:43:16,260 --> 00:43:18,262
[chattering indistinctly]

959
00:43:20,681 --> 00:43:22,391
What are you guys doing here?

960
00:43:22,474 --> 00:43:24,018
Welcome to your style consult.

961
00:43:24,101 --> 00:43:26,478
Lark didn't call you here. We did.

962
00:43:26,562 --> 00:43:28,731
We thought you all needed
more elevated looks, you know,

963
00:43:28,814 --> 00:43:30,733
so your performances will really pop.

964
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:35,070
All of you needed serious redesigning.

965
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:36,405
Desi,

966
00:43:36,488 --> 00:43:39,408
you'll never have what it takes
to shine on stage.

967
00:43:39,491 --> 00:43:41,577
But, hey, at least your sneakers will.

968
00:43:43,912 --> 00:43:45,080
Fletch.

969
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:47,916
Some preschool realness
for our mysterious musician.

970
00:43:49,376 --> 00:43:51,045
- Cliff.
- [Cliff] My drumsticks!

971
00:43:51,128 --> 00:43:52,504
Now, they're as weird as you are.

972
00:43:55,841 --> 00:43:57,676
Fix your branding problem, Sage.

973
00:43:57,760 --> 00:43:59,678
This is next level petty, Madison!

974
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:01,847
Whatever major loser!

975
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:07,019
And you know, Rosie,
classical music is just so stuffy.

976
