<i>♪ Swear I could write a thousand lines ♪</i>

1216
00:55:52,849 --> 00:55:54,934
<i>♪ About what I'm scared of ♪</i>

1217
00:55:55,018 --> 00:55:57,812
<i>♪ But face it now
I'mma find the light ♪</i>

1218
00:55:57,896 --> 00:56:00,565
<i>♪ Maybe I am strong enough ♪</i>

1219
00:56:00,648 --> 00:56:03,318
<i>♪ Keep going
I like the sound of it ♪</i>

1220
00:56:03,401 --> 00:56:07,781
<i>♪ Let's make it loud
'cause I hear it in my head ♪</i>

1221
00:56:07,864 --> 00:56:11,326
<i>- ♪ Like an echo, echo ♪
- ♪ I hear it ♪</i>

1222
00:56:11,409 --> 00:56:16,873
<i>♪ A song I can't forget
don't wanna let go, let go ♪</i>

1223
00:56:16,956 --> 00:56:19,751
<i>♪ And every person that I found ♪</i>

1224
00:56:19,834 --> 00:56:22,754
<i>♪ Is a melody that sticks around ♪</i>

1225
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:26,591
<i>♪ Like an e-e-e-echo ♪</i>

1226
00:56:26,674 --> 00:56:30,220
<i>♪ Like an echo ♪</i>

1227
00:56:33,556 --> 00:56:35,266
[all laughing]

1228
00:56:36,810 --> 00:56:37,977
[snores]

1229
00:56:41,689 --> 00:56:42,774
[snores]

1230
00:56:44,442 --> 00:56:46,236
[Sage] I'll never get over these stars.

1231
00:56:46,903 --> 00:56:48,405
I wish summer lasted forever.

1232
00:56:53,910 --> 00:56:54,994
Hello?

1233
00:56:55,745 --> 00:56:57,288
Earth to Fletch.

1234
00:56:57,372 --> 00:56:58,456
Sorry.

1235
00:56:59,707 --> 00:57:01,126
What were you thinking about?

1236
00:57:01,709 --> 00:57:02,710
Nothing.

1237
00:57:04,796 --> 00:57:06,047
Those eyes are dangerous.

1238
00:57:06,131 --> 00:57:08,007
[both laughing]

1239
00:57:08,967 --> 00:57:10,260
Um...

1240
00:57:11,219 --> 00:57:12,303
I was just

1241
00:57:14,139 --> 00:57:16,641
thinking about how winning
this competition could...

1242
00:57:17,600 --> 00:57:19,018
It could really fix everything.

1243
00:57:20,770 --> 00:57:23,606
I still have no idea where
I'm gonna be living after camp

1244
00:57:24,691 --> 00:57:26,693
but my cousin's fighting it for me.

1245
00:57:27,819 --> 00:57:31,865
I'm just waiting on the call to find out
where I'm headed next.

1246
00:57:35,660 --> 00:57:37,036
That's why I have this.

1247
00:57:41,124 --> 00:57:42,876
Well, I'm glad they let you
keep your phone.

1248
00:57:44,752 --> 00:57:45,753
Oh.

1249
00:57:47,213 --> 00:57:49,382
They didn't exactly let me keep my phone.

1250
00:57:49,466 --> 00:57:52,051
I showed up after registration
and no one asked.

1251
00:57:53,261 --> 00:57:54,345
Please don't...

1252
00:57:54,429 --> 00:57:55,555
Please don't say anything.

1253
00:57:55,638 --> 00:57:56,723
I won't.

1254
00:58:01,478 --> 00:58:02,604
[shivers]

1255
00:58:03,563 --> 00:58:04,647
Are you cold?

1256
00:58:05,148 --> 00:58:06,316
I'm good.

1257
00:58:08,234 --> 00:58:09,277
Right.

1258
00:58:09,360 --> 00:58:10,528
[laughs]

1259
00:58:12,822 --> 00:58:14,657
- Thanks. I appreciate it.
- Mm-hmm.

1260
00:58:18,119 --> 00:58:19,913
[owl hooting]

1261
00:58:26,753 --> 00:58:29,005
Why do you always sing
with your eyes closed?

1262
00:58:31,090 --> 00:58:33,259
Don't you want to connect with
the people in the audience?

1263
00:58:33,343 --> 00:58:34,677
And why?

1264
00:58:35,553 --> 00:58:37,764
They all leave after the show anyways.

1265
00:58:38,473 --> 00:58:39,724
I don't know, I...

1266
00:58:41,476 --> 00:58:44,604
I don't want the people
that I share a connection with to just...

1267
00:58:47,232 --> 00:58:48,274
leave.

1268
00:58:51,277 --> 00:58:54,489
Yeah, but what if it's worth it
to really connect with someone?

1269
00:58:55,865 --> 00:58:57,575
Even if it's only for one song.

1270
00:59:02,372 --> 00:59:04,207
[car horn honks]

1271
00:59:04,290 --> 00:59:07,710
- [others in bus] Cliff!
- [Cliff] Whoops! Sorry.

1272
00:59:07,794 --> 00:59:09,212
[both laughing]

1273
00:59:09,295 --> 00:59:10,547
[birds chirping]

1274
00:59:14,842 --> 00:59:16,094
[snoring]

1275
00:59:16,177 --> 00:59:17,178
[whistle blows]

1276
00:59:18,137 --> 00:59:20,056
Oh good. You guys are awake.

1277
00:59:20,139 --> 00:59:21,432
Your 24 hours are up.

1278
00:59:21,516 --> 00:59:23,893
Is this real or am I still hallucinating?

1279
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:26,396
This is very real. You're done!

1280
00:59:26,479 --> 00:59:28,481
Final Jam is tomorrow night.

1281
00:59:29,399 --> 00:59:32,443
That means you have
one day left to work on your songs.

1282
00:59:33,528 --> 00:59:34,571
Don't waste it.

1283
00:59:35,738 --> 00:59:36,990
You know where to find me.

1284
00:59:38,491 --> 00:59:41,494
Is it weird that I'm kinda
gonna miss this bus?

1285
00:59:41,578 --> 00:59:42,787
Not weird.

1286
00:59:44,330 --> 00:59:45,331
Same here.

1287
00:59:46,040 --> 00:59:47,500
[Sage] So we make a pact,

1288
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:49,669
whatever happens, we stay in touch.

1289
00:59:52,046 --> 00:59:54,382
[Cliff] Great. First order of business...

1290
00:59:55,133 --> 00:59:56,843
[yawns] Group chat name?

1291
00:59:58,136 --> 00:59:59,220
How about...

1292
01:00:00,305 --> 01:00:02,015
Cliff and the Cliffhangers?

1293
01:00:02,098 --> 01:00:04,601
- [all chuckle]
- Cliff.

1294
01:00:04,684 --> 01:00:06,311
We'll workshop it later.

1295
01:00:22,869 --> 01:00:23,870
[sighing]

1296
01:00:28,958 --> 01:00:30,376
I know that notebook.

1297
01:00:31,169 --> 01:00:34,547
Oh, wow. I have not seen it in so long.

1298
01:00:34,631 --> 01:00:35,715
It's been years.

1299
01:00:35,798 --> 01:00:37,300
I found it hidden in my cabin.

1300
01:00:38,426 --> 01:00:40,595
Whenever Mitchie
was dealing with something

1301
01:00:40,678 --> 01:00:43,556
or feeling something,
she just had to write about it.

1302
01:00:43,640 --> 01:00:45,266
It helped her figure things out.

1303
01:00:45,350 --> 01:00:47,977
Yeah, that's exactly
what it's been doing for me.

1304
01:00:48,061 --> 01:00:49,103
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

1305
01:00:49,187 --> 01:00:50,229
[chuckles softly]

1306
01:00:50,313 --> 01:00:52,398
But here. She probably wants it back.

1307
01:00:52,482 --> 01:00:54,901
- How about you take care of it for her?
- Really?

1308
01:00:54,984 --> 01:00:57,528
I think Mitchie would want it
to stay at Camp Rock.

1309
01:00:58,112 --> 01:01:00,615
With someone who needs it
just as much as she did.

1310
01:01:01,658 --> 01:01:03,201
How's the songwriting coming?

1311
01:01:03,868 --> 01:01:05,161
I'm not quite there yet.

1312
01:01:06,162 --> 01:01:07,705
That's okay.

1313
01:01:07,789 --> 01:01:09,123
It's a work in progress.

1314
01:01:14,921 --> 01:01:18,633
[♪ piano music playing]

1315
01:01:24,430 --> 01:01:26,391
[mumbling indistinctly]

1316
01:01:35,233 --> 01:01:37,443
[laughs, applauds]

1317
01:01:37,527 --> 01:01:38,861
Okay!

1318
01:01:38,945 --> 01:01:40,029
Go away.

1319
01:01:40,780 --> 01:01:42,448
When did you learn to dance?

1320
01:01:42,532 --> 01:01:45,410
Mmm, since you ditched me and the band,

1321
01:01:45,493 --> 01:01:46,994
I had a lot of free time.

1322
01:01:47,078 --> 01:01:48,955
I didn't ditch you. I just...

1323
01:01:49,038 --> 01:01:50,331
I wanted more than the garage.

1324
01:01:50,415 --> 01:01:54,085
Yeah, well, when you left for more,
you left me, too.

1325
01:01:56,337 --> 01:01:58,381
- Desi--
- I miss being your bandmate, Sage.

1326
01:02:00,049 --> 01:02:01,134
And your brother.

1327
01:02:01,884 --> 01:02:03,428
- In that order.
- [laughs]

1328
01:02:05,805 --> 01:02:07,932
Okay, so maybe we try again?

1329
01:02:08,015 --> 01:02:11,227
Different stage, bigger crowd.

1330
01:02:11,310 --> 01:02:13,312
You know, this could be our reunion tour.

1331
01:02:13,396 --> 01:02:15,440
Come on, band mates for life.

1332
01:02:17,734 --> 01:02:19,026
[laughing]

1333
01:02:19,110 --> 01:02:21,070
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1334
01:02:24,574 --> 01:02:26,492
<i>♪ Mmm, mmm, mmm, mmm ♪</i>

1335
01:02:26,576 --> 01:02:28,494
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah ♪</i>

1336
01:02:28,578 --> 01:02:31,164
<i>♪ Okay, so maybe I'm stubborn
tried to be tougher ♪</i>

1337
01:02:31,247 --> 01:02:33,958
<i>♪ But maybe it ain't always
gotta be like that ♪</i>

1338
01:02:34,041 --> 01:02:35,334
<i>♪ Been a little self-centered ♪</i>

1339
01:02:35,418 --> 01:02:37,545
<i>♪ You don't know the pressure
I was under ♪</i>

1340
01:02:37,628 --> 01:02:39,338
<i>♪ When you wouldn't hit me back ♪</i>

1341
01:02:39,422 --> 01:02:40,923
<i>♪ You talk fast when you're wrong ♪</i>

1342
01:02:41,007 --> 01:02:42,675
<i>♪ You hold grudges too long ♪</i>

1343
01:02:42,759 --> 01:02:44,218
<i>♪ Driving me insane! ♪</i>

1344
01:02:44,302 --> 01:02:45,887
<i>♪ Sorry for the cold shoulder ♪</i>

1345
01:02:45,970 --> 01:02:47,138
<i>♪ If I could do it over ♪</i>

1346
01:02:47,221 --> 01:02:50,349
<i>♪ I would go back
and take more of the blame ♪</i>

1347
01:02:50,433 --> 01:02:52,560
<i>♪ No matter how much that we're fightin' ♪</i>

1348
01:02:52,643 --> 01:02:55,146
<i>♪ And boy, don't you know
that we tried it ♪</i>

1349
01:02:55,229 --> 01:02:57,857
<i>♪ No matter how hard we deny it ♪</i>

1350
01:02:57,940 --> 01:02:59,734
<i>♪ Deny it ♪</i>

1351
01:02:59,817 --> 01:03:01,652
<i>♪ We got the same back beat heartbeat ♪</i>

1352
01:03:01,736 --> 01:03:03,863
<i>♪ No one do it like we do ♪</i>

1353
01:03:04,989 --> 01:03:10,703
<i>♪ We got the same tempo in our bones
Rockin' it like a groove ♪</i>

1354
01:03:10,787 --> 01:03:13,706
<i>♪ Ooh, we've been through a lot ♪</i>

1355
01:03:13,790 --> 01:03:15,333
<i>♪ Kinda hate that it's true ♪</i>

1356
01:03:15,416 --> 01:03:18,544
<i>♪ We got the same
back beat, heartbeat, yeah ♪</i>

1357
01:03:18,628 --> 01:03:21,506
<i>- ♪ Rhythm's only right with ♪
- ♪ Only right with ♪</i>

1358
01:03:21,589 --> 01:03:24,884
<i>♪ You, you, you, you ♪</i>

1359
01:03:26,385 --> 01:03:28,304
<i>♪ All the late nights ♪</i>

1360
01:03:28,387 --> 01:03:31,349
<i>♪ Always get into fights ♪</i>

1361
01:03:31,432 --> 01:03:35,019
<i>♪ But no one understands me like you do ♪</i>

1362
01:03:35,102 --> 01:03:36,437
<i>♪ Just keep on ♪</i>

1363
01:03:36,521 --> 01:03:38,105
<i>♪ Keep on rolling your eyes ♪</i>

1364
01:03:38,189 --> 01:03:41,567
<i>♪ You're stuck in this band for life ♪</i>

1365
01:03:41,651 --> 01:03:45,988
<i>♪ In the end
I'm glad it's me and you ♪</i>

1366
01:03:46,072 --> 01:03:48,407
<i>♪ Because we got the same
back beat, heart beat ♪</i>

1367
01:03:48,491 --> 01:03:50,368
<i>♪ No one do it like we do ♪</i>

1368
01:03:51,285 --> 01:03:53,371
<i>♪ We got the same tempo in our bones ♪</i>

1369
01:03:53,454 --> 01:03:55,248
<i>♪ Rockin' it like a groove ♪</i>

1370
01:03:57,542 --> 01:04:00,253
<i>♪ Ooh, we've been through a lot ♪</i>

1371
01:04:00,336 --> 01:04:01,838
<i>♪ Kinda hate that it's true ♪</i>

1372
01:04:01,921 --> 01:04:04,382
<i>♪ We got the same back beat heartbeat ♪</i>

1373
01:04:04,465 --> 01:04:06,676
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah
The rhythm's only right with ♪</i>

1374
01:04:06,759 --> 01:04:10,847
<i>♪ Only right with you, you, you, you ♪</i>

1375
01:04:11,389 --> 01:04:13,641
<i>♪ Rhythm's only with you ♪</i>

1376
01:04:13,724 --> 01:04:15,393
[PA chimes]

1377
01:04:15,935 --> 01:04:17,854
[Connie] <i>Will the final five</i>
<i>of the competition</i>

1378
01:04:17,937 --> 01:04:19,605
<i>please report to my office?</i>

1379
01:04:23,401 --> 01:04:24,735
Any idea what this is about?

1380
01:04:24,819 --> 01:04:25,903
No idea.

1381
01:04:31,576 --> 01:04:32,952
Come on in.

1382
01:04:33,035 --> 01:04:34,078
Have a seat.

1383
01:04:38,833 --> 01:04:40,376
I know that one of you has a phone.

1384
01:04:42,169 --> 01:04:43,462
Who is it?

1385
01:04:43,546 --> 01:04:44,589
You knew the rule.

1386
01:04:44,672 --> 01:04:48,259
No phones, no posting, no excuses.

1387
01:04:50,803 --> 01:04:52,680
I could disqualify all of you.

1388
01:04:52,763 --> 01:04:53,764
No!

1389
01:04:54,307 --> 01:04:55,308
[exhales]

1390
01:04:56,142 --> 01:04:57,143
[tapping nervously]

1391
01:04:57,226 --> 01:04:59,896
Well, I haven't seen my phone
since I turned it in.

1392
01:05:02,732 --> 01:05:03,983
Don't look at me.

1393
01:05:04,066 --> 01:05:05,735
My mom won't even let me have a phone.

1394
01:05:05,818 --> 01:05:08,446
She thinks I have focus issues,
which is ridiculous.

1395
01:05:10,197 --> 01:05:11,490
Sorry.

1396
01:05:11,574 --> 01:05:15,661
I may not take things seriously,
but I wouldn't break this rule.

1397
01:05:18,372 --> 01:05:19,540
That leaves you two.

1398
01:05:20,791 --> 01:05:23,044
[Lark] Guys, the competition's
on the line.

1399
01:05:23,127 --> 01:05:25,338
Connect 3 still needs an opening act.

1400
01:05:25,421 --> 01:05:28,382
Fletch... just tell them.

1401
01:05:31,093 --> 01:05:32,219
Are you being serious?

1402
01:05:32,303 --> 01:05:34,138
What is she talking about?

1403
01:05:36,807 --> 01:05:37,808
[sighs]

1404
01:05:40,186 --> 01:05:41,187
Uh...

1405
01:05:45,900 --> 01:05:47,109
[scoffs]

1406
01:05:48,152 --> 01:05:49,445
[groans softly]

1407
01:06:01,707 --> 01:06:03,793
I hope you're happy with yourself, Fletch.

1408
01:06:03,876 --> 01:06:07,672
A video of all of you singing on the bus
has already gone viral.

1409
01:06:08,798 --> 01:06:10,716
Yeah. I've been doing
damage control all day.

1410
01:06:10,800 --> 01:06:13,094
The brothers are not happy about this.

1411
01:06:13,177 --> 01:06:15,179
The competition was supposed
to be a big reveal.

1412
01:06:15,262 --> 01:06:16,430
No, wait! He...

1413
01:06:16,514 --> 01:06:17,723
He would never do that.

1414
01:06:18,474 --> 01:06:20,101
Everyone out!

1415
01:06:20,184 --> 01:06:21,268
Fletch, you stay.

1416
01:06:29,026 --> 01:06:31,070
- Fletch.
- [Connie] Sage.

1417
01:06:31,153 --> 01:06:33,406
- Go.
- [Fletch] Connie, it wasn't me, I swear.

1418
01:06:34,740 --> 01:06:38,035
[Connie] Well, if you didn't
post it, Fletch, then who did?

1419
01:06:39,704 --> 01:06:40,705
[♪ guitar strumming]

1420
01:06:47,169 --> 01:06:48,713
Be honest. Am I the worst?

1421
01:06:49,588 --> 01:06:50,756
Define worst.

1422
01:06:50,840 --> 01:06:52,216
Desi, be serious.

1423
01:06:52,842 --> 01:06:54,552
I mean, did Fletch have a phone?

1424
01:06:54,635 --> 01:06:55,720
Yeah.

1425
01:06:56,262 --> 01:06:58,305
But did you have to tell Connie about it?

1426
01:07:00,141 --> 01:07:02,393
I mean, we were all
gonna get disqualified.

1427
01:07:03,269 --> 01:07:04,895
I couldn't risk not competing.

1428
01:07:04,979 --> 01:07:07,523
I mean, everything I've ever worked for
would've been for nothing.

1429
01:07:08,691 --> 01:07:11,527
But... I did regret it after I said it.

1430
01:07:14,822 --> 01:07:16,323
Do you think he'll ever forgive me?

1431
01:07:16,907 --> 01:07:18,159
I forgave you, didn't I?

1432
01:07:20,036 --> 01:07:21,662
Sage, I love how ambitious you are.

1433
01:07:22,413 --> 01:07:24,915
Honestly, I've been trying
to be a little more like you lately.

1434
01:07:25,458 --> 01:07:26,792
[chuckles softly]

1435
01:07:27,543 --> 01:07:29,253
But you did choose Anthem over me.

1436
01:07:30,212 --> 01:07:32,757
And now you chose
the competition over Fletch.

1437
01:07:33,424 --> 01:07:36,093
I've just always put my dream
before everything else.

1438
01:07:37,928 --> 01:07:40,014
My music was all I ever needed.

1439
01:07:42,224 --> 01:07:45,853
But this time, it's the everything else
that I can't stop thinking about.

1440
01:07:48,397 --> 01:07:50,691
Everything or everyone?

1441
01:08:03,204 --> 01:08:05,498
I think the the studio here
looks a lot nicer than when we were here.

1442
01:08:05,581 --> 01:08:06,957
I know, it's insane.
They have four engineers.

1443
01:08:07,041 --> 01:08:08,375
Hold on. Lark.

1444
01:08:08,459 --> 01:08:10,086
Oh, hey, guys!

1445
01:08:10,169 --> 01:08:11,962
Sorry, I can't really talk right now.

1446
01:08:12,046 --> 01:08:15,549
You have me producing Final Jam
which is like a billion tiny shows in one

1447
01:08:15,633 --> 01:08:17,009
on a summer camp's budget. So...

1448
01:08:17,093 --> 01:08:19,261
We're pretty familiar
with what the Final Jam is.

1449
01:08:19,345 --> 01:08:21,263
Well, get ready for my Final Jam.

1450
01:08:21,847 --> 01:08:25,392
Lark, you let your hair down, literally.

1451
01:08:25,476 --> 01:08:27,686
How nice of you to notice, Jason.

1452
01:08:27,770 --> 01:08:32,191
I have bug bites on my bug bites
and a lot to discuss with my therapist.

1453
01:08:32,274 --> 01:08:33,651
You'll be getting the invoice.

1454
01:08:33,734 --> 01:08:36,987
Oh, come on, you're gonna miss this place.
You know you are.

1455
01:08:37,655 --> 01:08:39,031
I guess the songs are kinda catchy.

1456
01:08:39,115 --> 01:08:40,950
You know what? I don't have time for this.

1457
01:08:41,033 --> 01:08:43,202
I'm busy. I'll see you later.
Don't be late.

1458
01:08:43,285 --> 01:08:44,286
I saw that smile.

1459
01:08:45,788 --> 01:08:47,164
